WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.640
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:12.400
Today we are going to see what DeepMind’s AI is&nbsp;
able to do after being unleashed on the internet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:20.000
and reading no less than 2 trillion words.&nbsp;
And, amusingly, it also thinks that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.240
is a genius. So, is it? Well, we are&nbsp;
going to find out together today.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:34.480
I am really curious about that, especially given&nbsp;
how powerful these recent AI language models are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:40.720
For instance, OpenAI’s GPT-3&nbsp;
language model AI can now write poems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:49.040
and even continue your stories. And even&nbsp;
better, these stories can change direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:55.040
and the AI can still pick them up&nbsp;
and finish them. Recipes work too.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.160
So, while OpenAI is writing&nbsp;
these outstanding papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.800
I wonder what scientists at DeepMind are&nbsp;
up to these days? Well, check this out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:14.800
They have unleashed their AI that they call Gopher&nbsp;
on the internet and asked it to read as much as it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:23.120
can. That is, 2 trillion words. My goodness, that&nbsp;
is a ton of text. So, what did it learn from it?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:33.440
Oh boy, a great deal. But mostly, this one can&nbsp;
answer questions. Hmm…questions? There are plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:41.280
of AIs around that can answer questions. Some&nbsp;
can even solve a math exam straight from MIT.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:49.680
So, why is this so interesting? Well, while humans&nbsp;
are typically experts at one thing, or very few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:57.200
things, this AI is nearly an expert at almost&nbsp;
everything. Let’s see what it can do together!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.360
For instance, we can ask a bunch&nbsp;
of questions about biology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:08.000
and it will not only be quite insightful, but&nbsp;
it also remembers what we were discussing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.040
few questions ago. That is not trivial&nbsp;
at all. So cool! Now note that not all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.400
of its answers are completely correct. We will&nbsp;
have a more detailed look at that in a moment.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.680
Also, what I absolutely loved seeing when&nbsp;
reading the paper is that we can even ask what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:35.840
it is thinking. And look - it expresses that it&nbsp;
wishes to play on its smartphone. Very humanlike!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:44.000
Now make no mistake - that this does not mean&nbsp;
that this AI is thinking like a human is thinking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.520
At the risk of simplifying it, this is more&nbsp;
like a statistical combination of things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.320
that it had learned that people say on the&nbsp;
internet when asked what they are thinking.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.800
Now note that many of these new works are so&nbsp;
difficult to evaluate because they typically do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:07.280
better on some topics than previous ones,&nbsp;
and worse on others. The comparison of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.600
techniques can easily become a bit subjective&nbsp;
depending on what we are looking for. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:20.400
not here! Hold on to your papers,&nbsp;
and have a look at this! Oh wow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:31.200
My goodness! Are you seeing what I am seeing? This&nbsp;
is OpenAI’s GPT-3, and this is Gopher. As you see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.840
it is a great leap forward not just here and&nbsp;
there, but in many categories at the same time!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:47.200
Also, GPT-3 used 175 billion parameters&nbsp;
to train its neural network, Gopher uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:54.160
280 billion parameters, and you see, we get&nbsp;
plenty of value for these additional parameters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:01.360
So, what does all this mean? This means that&nbsp;
as these neural networks get bigger and bigger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.640
they are still getting better. We are steadily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:12.000
closing in on the human-level experts in many&nbsp;
areas at the same time, and progress is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.880
not plateauing. It still has more left in&nbsp;
the tank. How much more? We don’t know yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:26.000
but as you see, the pace of improvement in AI&nbsp;
research is absolutely incredible. However, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:33.200
are still not there yet. Its knowledge in the area&nbsp;
of humanities, social sciences and medicine is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:40.960
fantastic, but at mathematics, of all things, not&nbsp;
so much. You will see more about that in a moment.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:48.480
And, if you have been holding on to your papers,&nbsp;
now, squeeze that paper, because…would you look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:58.000
that! What is it that I am seeing here? Oh boy. It&nbsp;
thinks that it is a genius. Well, is it? Let’s ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:04.880
some challenging questions about Einstein’s field&nbsp;
equations, black holes and more and find out.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.240
Hmm. Well, it has a few things&nbsp;
going for it. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:16.560
it has a great deal of factual knowledge, however,&nbsp;
at the same time, it can also get quite confused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:23.200
by very simple questions. Do geniuses mess&nbsp;
up this multiplication? I should hope not!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:31.520
Also, have a look at this. We noted that it is not&nbsp;
much of a math wizard. When asked these questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:38.560
it gives us an answer, and when we ask are you&nbsp;
sure about that, it says it is very confident.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:45.440
But, it is confidently incorrect, I am afraid,&nbsp;
because none of these answers are correct.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:51.840
So, a genius AI? Well, not quite&nbsp;
yet. Human-level intelligence?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.560 --> 00:06:00.480
Also, not yet. But this is an incredible step&nbsp;
forward just one more paper down the line. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:06.080
just imagine what we will be able to do&nbsp;
just a couple more papers down the line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:11.280
What do you think? Does this get your mind going?&nbsp;
Let me know your ideas in the comments below!

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.680
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

